   "note": "YEAR CONFLICT SETTLED, and it closes a third series. Title page leaf 17 reads 'THE NEW-YORK CITY DIRECTORY, FOR 1854-1855. Thirteenth Publication. ESTABLISHED IN 1842. NEW-YORK: CHARLES R. RODE, 161 BROADWAY, LATE DOGGETT & RODE.' The catalog's 1851 is wrong. This volume PRINTS ITS OWN SERIES ORIGIN -- 'ESTABLISHED IN 1842' -- and the arithmetic matches Doggett exactly: Doggett's 4th is 1845, his 6th is 1847, Rode's 13th is 1854, and all three imply vol 1 in 1842. 'LATE DOGGETT & RODE' names the succession outright, so Doggett and Rode are ONE series. Leaf 16 is a Durst/Avery bookplate, which is why phase 0b's candidates missed this."
  },
